### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- metadata: {"openclaw":{"emoji":"📣","requires":{"bins":["python3"]},"install":[{"id":"brew-python","kind":"brew","formula":"python","bins":["python3"],"label":"Install Python 3 (brew)","os":["darwin"]}]}}
- - On Linux servers, preinstall `python3` with the system package manager before using this skill.
- 2. If there is no valid local session, run `scripts/publisher_cli.py prepare-login` first.
- 3. Prefer the inline QR image fields returned by `prepare-login`: send `chat_image.base64` or `qr_png_data_url` directly in chat, then tell the user exactly: `请使用 Z视介 APP 扫描此二维码登录。`
- 4. After the QR image has been shown in chat, run `scripts/publisher_cli.py wait-login` with the returned `qr_state_file` and wait for scan completion.
- 5. Only fall back to attaching `qr_png_file` when the runtime supports local image attachments but inline base64 delivery is unavailable.
- 6. Do not send only a local file path string to Feishu/Lark chat. The QR image must be sent as actual image content.
- 7. Do not surface the internal QR login API details unless the user explicitly asks for them.
- 8. Build the exact request body as a JSON file matching the operation docs. Pass it with `--input-json`.
- 9. Run one of `publish-article`, `edit-article`, `publish-video`, or `edit-video`.
- 10. If the publish host differs from the bundled default, override it with `--base-url`.
- 11. Run `scripts/release_to_clawhub.py` before sharing the skill on ClawHub. Use `--execute` only when `clawhub` is installed and already authenticated.
